        "install.manual": "Open your browser menu → Install app / Add to Home Screen",
        "about.histoHtml": "<h4>Observations-per-day bar chart</h4><p>With observations on the map, a slim bar chart docks under it: one bar per day, from the oldest plotted observation to today (right end), horizontally scrollable with dates along the bottom. Faint stubs mark days without observations (toggleable in Settings). <b>Hover</b> a bar to preview just that day on the map and in the legend — and hovering a species in the legend previews its days here. <b>Click</b> a bar (it turns orange) to add that date to the filters; click more days to combine, click again to remove. The ▾ handle collapses the chart to a slim band (tap the band to reopen); a new fetch reopens it automatically. The bars count only the observations inside the current map view (re-counted as you pan/zoom), honouring the species selection and active filters.</p>",
        "about.rarityHtml": "<h4>eBird rarity alerts</h4><p>Save a location (right-click the map → Save location), press-and-hold the 🔍 search button and tick its <b>🔔</b> column. While the app is open it then checks eBird's <i>notable sightings</i> feed there (within max 50 km) at the interval you choose — new rarities appear as pulsing red <b>★</b> on the map and under the header bell, with an alarm chirp and optional system notifications (Settings → Rarity alerts; needs the free eBird API key). The very first check of a location arms silently, so subscribing never sets off a storm of old alerts. The app cannot alert while the browser is closed.</p>",
        "about.creditsHtml": "<h4>Credits &amp; licence</h4><p><b>BirdsWhere</b> &mdash; application code under the <b>MIT</b> licence. &copy; 2026. Reuse is welcome <b>with attribution</b>; where a component is share-alike, derivatives must keep the same licence.</p><p><b>Species model.</b> <a href=\"https://github.com/birdnet-team/geomodel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BirdNET Geomodel</a> by the BirdNET team &mdash; K. Lisa Yang Center for Conservation Bioacoustics (Cornell University), Chemnitz University of Technology and Museum f&uuml;r Naturkunde Berlin. Source MIT; the trained weights shipped with this app are <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a> and redistributed under those terms. <b>Powered by BirdNET.</b> The model licence forbids use for poaching or for any military purpose, and model output is a probabilistic prediction &mdash; not a confirmed observation.</p><p><b>Observations</b> &copy; their providers: eBird / Cornell Lab of Ornithology, GBIF, iNaturalist, Artsdatabanken, SLU Artdatabanken, FinBIF / Laji.fi, BirdWeather and Observation.org. Each is queried live from your device; nothing is redistributed here.</p><p><b>Maps</b> &copy; OpenStreetMap contributors, &copy; CARTO, OpenTopoMap, Esri, MapTiler and OpenFreeMap. <b>Overlays</b>: protected areas from UNEP-WCMC &amp; IUCN (WDPA &mdash; non-commercial use, attribution required), Natura 2000 from the EEA, and Ramsar sites.</p><p><b>Migration Aloft</b> uses weather-radar profiles from <a href=\"https://aloftdata.eu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">aloftdata.eu</a> (<a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY 4.0</a>), weather from <a href=\"https://www.ecmwf.int/en/forecasts/datasets/open-data\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ECMWF Open Data</a> (CC BY 4.0 &mdash; please attribute ECMWF), and coastlines from Natural Earth (public domain). Its species-turnover layer is derived from BirdNET Geomodel output and is therefore offered under CC BY-SA 4.0.</p><p><b>Bundled libraries</b>: Leaflet (BSD-2-Clause), MapLibre GL (BSD-3-Clause), ONNX Runtime Web (MIT), h3-js (Apache-2.0). Full third-party notices accompany the source repository.</p>",
        "about.installHtml": "<h4>📲 Install for offline use</h4><p>Install it once while online — then it runs with no signal.</p><p><b>iPhone / iPad:</b> open this page in <b>Safari</b> (iOS 11.3 or newer), tap <b>Share</b> ⎙, then <b>Add to Home Screen</b>. On iPhone only Safari can install web apps.</p><p><b>Android:</b> in <b>Chrome</b> (or Edge / Firefox / Brave) open the <b>⋮ menu → Install app</b> (or “Add to Home screen”); or tap the app’s <b>Offline mode</b> button when it appears.</p><p>Open the app online at least once so it can store itself. For offline maps, download the areas you need first (use the ⤓ button on the map — press and hold it to manage saved areas).</p>",
        "install.done": "App installed ✓",
