        "maphelp.legend": "Legend. The plotted species, ordered by the model's predicted probability (low → high). Top buttons: − minimise to a corner chip; ☰ open the detections list (where the time, species and observer filters live); a black × clears the active filters (long-press or right-click it to open a panel of every filter, showing which are active); a red × removes every plotted detection (arms per-area delete when fetched-area outlines exist); ⚠ appears when the draw cap (Settings → Max points) is hiding dots. The list shows only species with a dot on screen; the number after each is how many of its specimens are on screen (passing the filters), and the top “Total” row sums that across all species (n of the grand total). Tap a species row to toggle it on/off — picks stack, so several show together; hover a row to isolate that species on the map. Long-press (or right-click) a species name for its menu.",
